      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fulda was founded in 1881 along the Milwaukee Road by German settlers, along with Scandinavians and Irish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulda%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from Fulda in Hessen, Germany, echoing the heritage of its early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulda%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A two‑story depot built for the Milwaukee Road still stands, its lower level now an antiques museum and store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulda%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fulda Memorial Library, opened in 1970, joined the Plum Creek Library System in 1975, serving the community for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulda%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A three‑inch Civil War cannon sits in Fulda’s city park, a relic from 1892 purchased by the local Grand Army of the Republic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulda%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Fulda remains a predominantly agricultural community, growing up alongside the railroad and preserving its rural character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
